INT. FAMILY MINIVAN - DRIVE-THROUGH BREAKFAST LANE - MORNING

Rain on the windshield. Four people. One bag of hash browns that has already been opened.

He is at the wheel, shouting into the speaker box while checking the mirror, the clock, and his phone all at once. His name is ROLAND ESPINOZA-HART (40s, tie half-knotted).

She is in the passenger seat, shouting over him to the speaker box, with a coffee in one hand and a sleeping bag stuffed under her arm. This is NEELAM ESPINOZA-HART (40s, hospital scrubs).

In the back, a girl of twelve, TAMSIN, kicks the seat. A boy of seven, FELIX, is standing on the seat, pressing his nose to the glass. A sibling war has broken out over the hash browns. They each have one hand in the bag and one hand on the other's face. Roland reaches back without looking and swats at both. Neelam reaches back, too, and her coffee spills down Roland's sleeve. He yelps. Tamsin shrieks. Felix falls off the seat onto the floor, still holding the bag.

ROLAND
Two number threes!

NEELAM
Three!

TAMSIN
He's eating mine!

FELIX
It's MY bag!

ROLAND
Everybody stop!

Nobody stops. The speaker box crackles. The car behind them honks.

NEELAM
Roland, move up.

ROLAND
I'm moving!

He is not moving. He is reaching for a napkin. Felix's foot is on the horn. The honk goes long. Neelam lunges for the foot. Tamsin grabs the napkin. Roland swerves a half inch and hits the speaker post.

The speaker box goes silent. All four freeze, mid-motion, a family in tableau. Then everyone starts again.
